==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la}} {{term|lang=la|turbulentus}} < {{term|lang=la|turba||disorder, tumult}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-turbulent.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# violently [[disturbed]] or [[agitated]]; [[tempestuous]], [[tumultuous]]
#: ''It is dangerous to sail in '''turbulent''' seas.''
# being in, or causing, [[disturbance]] or [[unrest]]
#: ''The mid-19th century was a '''turbulent''' time in American history.

